   \]
   Since H\(_2\)SO\(_4\) is diprotic, 1 mole provides 2 equivalents. Thus, the equivalents are equal to:
   \[
   20.0 \, \text{eq} = 10.0 \, \text{mol}
   \]

2. **Calculate the total equivalents of H\(_2\)SO\(_4\) in the final solution:**
   \[
   \text{Equivalents} = \text{Molarity} \times \text{Volume (L)} = 3.00 \, \text{M} \times 20.0 \, \text{L} = 60.0 \, \text{eq}
   \]
   \[
   60.0 \, \text{eq} = 30.0 \, \text{mol}
   \]

