\]
Substituting the expressions for $f(x - \frac{\pi}{12})$ and $f(1 - x - \frac{\pi}{12})$:
\[
\sin \left( \omega (x - \frac{\pi}{12}) + \varphi \right) = -\sin \left( \omega (1 - x - \frac{\pi}{12}) + \varphi \right).
\]
Using the identity $\sin(-\theta) = -\sin(\theta)$, we get:
\[
\sin \left( \omega (x - \frac{\pi}{12}) + \varphi \right) = \sin \left( \omega (x + \frac{\pi}{12}) - \varphi \right).
\]
