Let's assume the new time frame is \( x \) years. The number of people in the first time frame is \( 5 \times 3600 \) (since there are 3600 minutes in a year). The number of people in the second time frame is \( x \times 3600 \).

The difference in the number of people in the two time frames is \( x \times 3600 - 5 \times 3600 = 3600(x - 5) \).

Since the new time frame is longer, the total amount will be higher. The difference in the total amount will be \( 150 \times 3600 \) (since the new time frame is longer, the total amount will be higher).

Setting up the equation:
\[
