1. **List all possible combinations**:
   \[
   \begin{array}{|cccc|}
   P & Q & R & P \rightarrow Q & Q \rightarrow R \\
   \hline
   \text{I} & \text{I} & \text{I} & \hline
   \text{I} & \text{I} & \text{N} & \hline
   \text{I} & \text{N} & \text{I} & \hline
   \text{I} & \text{N} & \text{N} & \hline
   \text{N} & \text{I} & \text{I} & \hline
   \text{N} & \text{I} & \text{N} & \hline
   \text{N} & \text{N} & \text{I} & \hline
   \text{N} & \text{N} & \text{N} & \hline
   \end{array}
   \]

2. **Compute the truth values for \( P \rightarrow Q \) and \( Q \rightarrow R \)**:
