   The matrix \( H \) satisfies that \( H(H \cdot \lambda) = H \cdot (H \cdot \lambda) \) for any \( \lambda \) in the row space of \( H \).

2. **Basis of \( C \)**:
   The matrix \( H \) is a basis of \( C \), meaning \( C \) is spanned by the \( a_i \). The matrix \( H \) is also linearly dependent, so there exists a linear combination of \( a_i \) that is the zero vector.

