\[
|\lambda| = \left|1 - \frac{2\kappa \Delta t}{(\Delta x)^2} (1 - \cos(\pi \Delta x / \Delta t))\right|.
\]
The eigenvalues are independent of \(\Delta t\) and \(\Delta x\), and their absolute value is less than 1 for all \(\Delta t\). Therefore, the Dufort–Frankel method is stable for any \(\Delta t\). 

