   - Force due to the mass of the piston: \( mg = 25 \text{ kg} \times 9.807 \text{ m/s}^2 \).
   - Force due to atmospheric pressure: \( P_{\text{atm}} \times \frac{\pi}{4} d_A^2 \), where \( P_{\text{atm}} = 100 \text{ kPa} \).

2. **Equilibrium condition:**
   \[
   P_A \times \frac{\pi}{4} d_A^2 - P_B \times \frac{\pi}{4} d_B^2 - mg - P_{\text{atm}} \times \frac{\pi}{4} d_A^2 = 0
   \]
   Simplifying:
   \[
   P_A - P_B - \frac{mg}{\frac{\pi}{4} d_B^2} - P_{\text{atm}} = 0
   \]
   Substituting the given values:
   \[
   500 \text{ kPa} - P_B - \frac{25 \text{ kg} \times 9.807 \text{ m/s}^2}{\frac{\pi}{4} \times (0.025 \text{ m})^2} - 100 \text{ kPa} = 0
