","(a) The electric force on the proton is given by \(F = qE\), where \(q\) is the charge of the proton and \(E\) is the electric field strength. The net force on the proton is the electric force, so \(F = 1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C} \times 500 \, \text{N/C} = 7.00 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{N}\).  
The acceleration of the proton is then \(a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{9.00 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} = 5.18 \times 10^7 \, \text{m/s}^2\).  

(b) The time taken by the proton to reach a speed of \(35,000 \, \text{m/s}\) is calculated using the kinematic equation \(v = u + at\), where \(v\) is the final velocity, \(u\) is the initial velocity (0 m/s), \(a\) is the acceleration, and \(t\) is the time. Solving for \(t\):  
\[
t = \frac{v - u}{a} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s} - 0 \, \text{m/s}}{5.18 \times 10^7 \, \text{m/s}^2} = 6.25 \times 10^{-4} \, \text{s}.
\]  
The time required is \(\boxed{6.25 \times 10^{-4} \, \text{s}}\).
