","The entropy production rate \( \Pi_S \) is given by:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{Q}{T}
\]
where \( Q \) is the rate of heat transfer. In this process, the heat transfer is due to the work done by the friction force \( F_{\text{fr}} \) over the relative velocity \( v \). The work done per unit time is:
\[
\frac{dW}{dt} = F_{\text{fr}} v
\]
The heat transfer \( Q \) is equal to the work done:
\[
Q = \frac{dW}{dt} = F_{\text{fr}} v
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{Q}{T} = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}
\]
The entropy production rate is \(\boxed{\dfrac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}}\).
